ailed**.\n\n## Stage 3E — candidate corpus and tokenizer coverage\n\nComplete.\n\n- Added a read-only extractor over the same ten Hausa-bearing field names used\n  by the verified slice-35 audit.\n- Output is self-labelled `candidate_corpus_not_gold`, `goldStandard: false`;\n  every entry has `reviewStatus: candidate`.\n- 26 normalized-word candidates cover all 31 required labels, including all\n  fixed consonants, the four apostrophe/boundary classes, vowel/diphthong\n  ambiguity, native vs Arabic lexical `h`, proper nouns, acronyms, numerals, and\n  mixed-language contexts. Missing required labels: **0**.\n- Identical normalized words are deduplicated. Each retains total\n  `occurrenceCount` and up to 12 distinct references with source file, full\n  field path, module ID, source word, and complete surrounding sentence.\n- Proposed tokenization comes only from the existing verified tokenizer.\n  Provisional Ajami uses `canonical-mapping.json` plus the standard's approved\n  short-mark inventory as an explicitly incomplete review aid. The output\n  retains completeness and unresolved-decision fields and cannot approve itself.\n- Candidate extractor tests: **4 passed, 0 failed**.\n\n### Full tokenizer/corpus statistics\n\n- Hausa fields scanned: **7,227**\n- Unique normalized words: **3,243**\n- Known phoneme/vowel tokens: **977,529**\n- Unknown-token occurrences: **1,294**\n- Tokenization coverage: **99.8678%**\n- Actual unknown tokens:\n  - `P` U+0050: **936**\n  - `p` U+0070: **178**\n  - `x` U+0078: **78**\n  - `q` U+0071: **48**\n  - `V` U+0056: **37**\n  - `v` U+0076: **12**\n  - `ā` U+0101: **5**\n- Fixed-consonant token occurrences:\n  - `ɓ`: **1,184**\n  - `ɗ`: **6,298**\n  - `ƙ`: **6,391**\n  - `ƴ` / apostrophe-`y` abstract token: **326**\n  - `c`: **11,245**\n  - `ts`: **4,150**\n  - `sh`: **4,899**\n  - `f`: **13,079**\n  - `n`: **82,672**\n  - plain `k`: **56,720**\n  - plain `y`: **35,645**\n- Provisional fallback produced at least a partial review string for **3,194**\n  indexed normalized forms; **25/26** selected candidates have a partial\n  fallback. A fallback is not a verified spelling.\n- Arabic/Islamic-context heuristic: **138 unique words / 1,058 occurrences**.\n- Mixed Hausa–English-context heuristic: **430 unique words / 2,937 occurrences**.\n- Acronym candidates: **18 unique forms / 244 occurrences**.\n\n### Apostrophe carry-over\n\n- Total occurrences: **3,082**\n- Settled apostrophe-`y`: **254**\n- Still queued for review: **2,828**\n- Classifier categories: glottal boundary **1,801**; ambiguous **837**;\n  apostrophe-`y` **254**; paired quotation **150**; unpaired typographic\n  punctuation **37**; morpheme boundary **3**.\n\n## Stage 3F — Unicode hygiene validator\n\nComplete.\n\n- Added a non-mutating string validator plus recursive read-only\n  `app/content.json` scanner. Every finding records file, full field path,\n  entity ID, original string, full code-point sequence, violated rule, evidence\n  positions, and recommended disposition.\n- Synthetic tests cover presentation forms, PUA, U+FFFD, Latin+Arabic marks,\n  marks without Arabic bases, mark order, NFC instability, constructed\n  U+06DB substitutes, mixed canonical/noncanonical forms, new-output U+06D1,\n  native-Hausa `ه` classification, unconverted special letters/apostrophe-`y`,\n  and unsupported extended glyphs.\n- `U+06D1` is blocked only in `newlyGenerated` mode. It is not mislabeled\n  malformed during stored/import analysis.\n- Live scan: **15,717 strings**, including **315 Ajami fields**.\n- Findings: **646 rule findings across 289 fields**. These include confirmed\n  malformed Unicode and review-required orthographic/context findings; the\n  latter are not silently promoted to confirmed spelling errors.\n- Rule counts:\n  - mixed canonical/noncanonical native-Hausa output: **251 fields**\n  - unsupported extended Arabic glyph: **85 fields**\n  - invalid combining-mark order: **83 fields**\n  - NFC instability: **83 fields**\n  